!docs/reference/

# The RFC compliance references are tracked while the rest of docs/archive/ stays local. They call themselves
# the binding reference for this SDK's development and are cited by name in commit messages and reviews, so
# they have to be diffable and reviewable like the code they describe. Leaving them untracked is how they came
# to claim RFC 3261 §19.1.4 was done while its implementation was wrong in half the RFC's own examples (#336):
# nothing to diff, nothing to review, and no gate that could go red. The other files here stay ignored.
!docs/archive/
docs/archive/*
!docs/archive/status-raw/
docs/archive/status-raw/*
!docs/archive/status-raw/RFC_VOIP_SDK_COMPLIANCE.md
!docs/archive/status-raw/RFC3261_CHAPTER_STATUS.md

AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
VoipSdk_Targetstruktur_fuer_KI.md

scripts/*
!scripts/test-interop-browser-safe.sh
!scripts/prepare-release.sh
TestResults

# Commercial-module examples depend on paid modules not present in the open SDK; keep their
# non-building project sources out of the repo until those modules ship (README stays tracked).
examples/commercial/CalloraVoipSdk.Sample.Conference/
examples/commercial/CalloraVoipSdk.Sample.RealtimeBridge/

website/

# Git worktree scaffolding created by local tooling (e.g. agent worktrees).
.worktrees/
.claire/
